\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The deception-release wave. (a)~E15: per-attempt attacker success by release policy---decoy $0.000$ (stable under public verification), honest $1.000$, silence $0.200$; the decoy edge collapses monotonically as held-out capability arrives. (b)~E16: minimum held-out budget for gaming-gap detection at 95\% power vs.\ discrimination error $m$ ($m\ge 0.5$ half of the grid); beyond $m\approx 0.94$ no feasible budget reaches the power, while any misclassification \emph  {toward} the public support fails the public certificate immediately.}}{19}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:release}{{4}{19}{The deception-release wave. (a)~E15: per-attempt attacker success by release policy---decoy $0.000$ (stable under public verification), honest $1.000$, silence $0.200$; the decoy edge collapses monotonically as held-out capability arrives. (b)~E16: minimum held-out budget for gaming-gap detection at 95\% power vs.\ discrimination error $m$ ($m\ge 0.5$ half of the grid); beyond $m\approx 0.94$ no feasible budget reaches the power, while any misclassification \emph {toward} the public support fails the public certificate immediately}{figure.4}{}}
